Add a `-solution <file>` option to AILS-II so the routes can be checked.

Applied to https://github.com/INFORMSJoC/2023.0106 (AILS-II, Máximo, Cordeau,
Nascimento), which otherwise prints only a cost line — leaving its numbers as
the only ones in this repository that could not be independently revalidated.

The change is confined to main(): it reads one extra argument directly from
argv, without touching InputParameters, and writes the best solution through
the Solution.toString() that already exists. Solution.toString() emits
"Route #k: a b c" lines followed by "Cost <f>", i.e. exactly the CVRPLib .sol
format, with the depot as node 0 and customers numbered 1..n. No search
parameter, no acceptance rule and no operator is touched, so the trajectory is
bit-identical to the unpatched code.

A real unified diff with line numbers, so GNU patch, BSD patch and
`git apply -p0` all accept it.

Apply with:
    patch -p0 -d external/AILS-II < tools/ails_solution_output.patch

--- src/SearchMethod/AILSII.java
+++ src/SearchMethod/AILSII.java
@@ -207,6 +207,27 @@
 		AILSII ailsII=new AILSII(instance,reader);
 		
 		ailsII.search();
+
+		// -solution <file>: write the best solution in CVRPLib .sol format.
+		// Read straight from argv so InputParameters is left untouched.
+		String solutionFile=null;
+		for(int i=0;i<args.length-1;i++)
+			if(args[i].equals("-solution"))
+				solutionFile=args[i+1];
+		if(solutionFile!=null)
+		{
+			try
+			{
+				java.io.PrintWriter out=new java.io.PrintWriter(solutionFile);
+				out.print(ailsII.getBestSolution().toString());
+				out.close();
+			}
+			catch(java.io.IOException e)
+			{
+				System.err.println("could not write "+solutionFile+": "+e);
+				System.exit(1);
+			}
+		}
 	}
 	
 	public Solution getBestSolution() {
